' Feature-IQ use-case diagrams: full entry-point surface by actor.
' Companion to architecture.md and sequence-diagrams.puml.
'
' Render with: plantuml use-case-diagrams.puml   (emits one image per @startuml block)
'
' Permission model has TWO orthogonal axes (see backend/app/models/user.py and
' backend/app/models/competitor_intelligence.py):
'   1. Global UserRole: VOTER < PRODUCT_OWNER < ADMIN (role inheritance)
'   2. Per-product ProductPermissionLevel: VIEW < EDIT < OWNER
' Most product-scoped endpoints gate on axis 2 (verify_product_access in
' app/api/deps.py), regardless of global role. Axis 1 gates admin surfaces,
' MCP API-key creation, and a few PO-or-admin endpoints.

@startuml end-user-surface
title End-user surface — roles x entry points
left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam usecaseFontSize 12

actor Voter
actor "Product Owner" as PO
actor Admin
Voter <|-- PO
PO <|-- Admin

note bottom of Admin
  Global **UserRole** (axis 1).
  Arrows = role inheritance:
  PO can do everything Voter can;
  Admin everything PO can.
  Bracketed tags on use cases =
  per-product **ProductPermissionLevel**
  required (axis 2).
end note

rectangle "Feature-IQ (FastAPI backend + React frontend)" {

  package "Auth & profile  (/auth)" {
    usecase "Register / Login\n(+ optional TOTP MFA)" as UC_auth
    usecase "Manage profile,\npassword, MFA" as UC_profile
  }

  package "Ideas & voting  (/submissions /ideas /votes)" {
    usecase "Submit idea\n(triggers AI triage)" as UC_submit
    usecase "Vote on ideas\n(board ideas only,\nnot imported)" as UC_vote
    usecase "Comment & respond" as UC_comment
    usecase "Browse / search ideas\n[VIEW]" as UC_browse
  }

  package "PM review  (/pm-review)" {
    usecase "Triage review queue:\napprove / reject / defer / batch\n[EDIT]" as UC_pmreview
  }

  package "Product & job map  (/product-intelligence/products)" {
    usecase "Create / update product,\ntarget customer, scoring,\ntriage settings\n[EDIT]" as UC_product
    usecase "Job map: extract, edit,\nreview suggestions\n[EDIT]" as UC_jobmap
  }

  package "Competitive intelligence  (/product-intelligence/agents /monitoring)" {
    usecase "Manage competitor roster\n(add, track, deactivate)\n[EDIT]" as UC_roster
    usecase "Run audits, discovery,\nresearch refresh\n[EDIT]" as UC_audit
    usecase "View reports, alerts,\njob comparisons\n[VIEW]" as UC_reports
  }

  package "Synthesis  (/products .../synthesis)" {
    usecase "Configure + run\nunified synthesis\n[EDIT]" as UC_synth
    usecase "View scorecards,\nopportunities, recommendations\n[VIEW]" as UC_synthview
  }

  package "Evidence & internal feedback  (/product-intelligence /internal-feedback)" {
    usecase "Add / manage evidence,\nsubmit internal feedback\n[EDIT]" as UC_evidence
    usecase "View signals, themes,\nactivity insights\n[VIEW]" as UC_signals
  }

  package "Membership & invites  (/invites)" {
    usecase "Invite members,\nchange permission levels\n[OWNER]" as UC_invite
  }

  package "MCP access  (/api-keys)" {
    usecase "Create / revoke MCP API keys\n(PRODUCT_OWNER or ADMIN role)" as UC_apikeys
  }
}

Voter --> UC_auth
Voter --> UC_profile
Voter --> UC_submit
Voter --> UC_vote
Voter --> UC_comment
Voter --> UC_browse

PO --> UC_pmreview
PO --> UC_product
PO --> UC_jobmap
PO --> UC_roster
PO --> UC_audit
PO --> UC_reports
PO --> UC_synth
PO --> UC_synthview
PO --> UC_evidence
PO --> UC_signals
PO --> UC_invite
PO --> UC_apikeys

note bottom of UC_pmreview
  VOTER role is capped at VIEW by a
  central gate in PermissionService,
  so every EDIT-tagged use case
  effectively requires PO/ADMIN role
  + the product permission. Grants of
  edit/owner to voters are rejected
  at grant time.
end note
@enduml


@startuml admin-system-surface
title Admin & system surface — non-end-user entry points
left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam usecaseFontSize 12

actor Admin
actor "MCP client\n(Claude / agents)" as MCP
control "Celery Beat\n(daily tick)" as Beat

rectangle "Feature-IQ backend" {

  package "User administration  (/auth admin endpoints)" {
    usecase "Create / deactivate users,\nchange roles, assign products" as UC_users
    usecase "Reset passwords +\ninvalidate sessions\n(tokens_valid_after)" as UC_reset
    usecase "Unlock accounts,\nview login history\n(lockout: 5 fails / 15 min)" as UC_unlock
  }

  package "Operations  (/admin)" {
    usecase "Cost reporting: daily trends,\nper-user / product / model\nbreakdowns" as UC_costs
    usecase "Manage idea lifecycle\nstatuses" as UC_lifecycle
  }

  package "MCP server  (backend/mcp_server, 78 tools)" {
    usecase "Authenticate:\nOAuth 2.0 (HTTP, RFC 9728)\nor API-key bearer (stdio/HTTP)" as UC_mcpauth
    usecase "Product / ideas / CI /\nsynthesis / evidence tools\n(same per-product permission\nchecks as the REST API)" as UC_mcptools
    usecase "Dispatch async jobs +\npoll job_get_status\n(same Celery machinery)" as UC_mcpjobs
  }

  package "Scheduled agents  (app/queue/scheduled_tasks.py)" {
    usecase "check_scheduled_tasks (daily):\nqueue product analysis,\ncompetitor discovery, audits\nper CompetitiveAgentConfig" as UC_sched
  }
}

Admin --> UC_users
Admin --> UC_reset
Admin --> UC_unlock
Admin --> UC_costs
Admin --> UC_lifecycle

MCP --> UC_mcpauth
MCP --> UC_mcptools
MCP --> UC_mcpjobs

Beat --> UC_sched

note bottom of UC_mcptools
  MCP tools act as the user who owns
  the API key / OAuth grant — axis-2
  product permissions apply unchanged
  (mcp_server/permissions.py).
end note

note bottom of UC_sched
  No human actor: Beat fires daily;
  per-product schedule config decides
  what is due (daily/weekly/biweekly/
  monthly). Jobs enter the same
  Celery queues as user-triggered runs.
end note
@enduml
